{
  "description": "Device-authorization transition log served by GET /identity-devices/{identityId}/transitions (#513). Each log is what one node stores for the identity: the recovery lineage of its replay base, the recoveries that lost that checkpoint and the accepted history in replay order, every entry in the exact primitives of device-authorization-transition-vectors.json. The genesis is DeviceAuthorization.genesis(identityId, networkIds, keys.author, keys.recoveryAuthority), which a client derives from identity version 1. reads pin the body the node serves to an authenticated reader (a device key name for a device proof, recoveryAuthority for a recovery proof) for an after revision. verdicts pin the client decision on a served body: removedBy is the operationId of the signed transition that removed the reader after its local verified epoch and revision, or null when the body proves no removal (absence, truncation, a stale or forged removal never count).",
